    "generation": {
      "status": "ok",
      "text": "The policy applies to employees, contractors, interns, suppliers, and any other person who writes, builds, packages, deploys, or distributes software on behalf of the enterprise. It covers source code, binaries, packages, container images, model weights, firmware components, snippets copied from public repositories, transitive dependencies, build plugins, command-line tools, and OSS used in internal systems, customer products, demonstrations, prototypes, or production services. Exceptions MUST identify the component, version, license, business justification, compensating controls, vulnerability status, distribution model, legal assessment where relevant, accountable owner, and expiration date. Open-ended exceptions are prohibited. Critical-risk exceptions require CISO approval; material license exceptions require Legal approval. An exception MUST NOT be interpreted as permanent policy change. The control owner may require additional monitoring, narrower scope, remediation milestones, or earlier review. Expired exceptions automatically cease to authorize the deviation.",
